    {
      "topic": "Settled receipt replay",
      "result": "NO_SCANNER_APPEND_OR_NEW_RECEIPT_BRANCH",
      "detail": "The settled branch reopens cases.read even when lightweight authorizeCase exists; validates exact outbox/ledger event, committed record/eventId/recordDigest, capture and every source; repeats case and source observations; places final host revalidation inside the protected state.read callback. It returns the existing receipt as already-committed and exits before the new-emission scanner/state.transaction branch."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Installed wrapper recursion",
      "result": "PRIVATE_LOOKUP_SCOPE_WITHOUT_PUBLIC_AUTHORITY_CACHE",
      "detail": "A factory-local AsyncLocalStorage scope surrounds only caseForEvidence. The shortcut requires active scope, identical call/digest, stable Request, headers, binding and opaque lease. Its finally clears active. It calls canonicalMemory.readOriginalCapture directly, so the existing installed caseForEvidence -> memory.readOriginal callback does not reenter the full public authorization wrapper. Independent public calls outside that async scope execute the complete reader; late inherited scope calls fail closed."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Independent observations",
      "result": "RETAINED",
